# A symbol handed to `send` from another file runs the method, as a call
# does: Base#hook_a and Base#guarded came out `convention-only`, "named
# only by a symbol handed to a macro", which a macro's symbol is and a
# send's is not. Typed, it runs the method its receiver's lookup finds:
# `Other.new.send(:b1)` is no call of Foo#b1 (which stays as it was, named
# by the symbol), and `send(:a2)` in a class body is the singleton's.
# Hooked#on_save, a macro's and sent by a spec, is single-caller: the
# macro's symbol goes unsaid beside a call (DEC-664, not done).
dead app Base#hook_a=single-caller Base#guarded=single-caller Other#b1=single-caller~ Foo#b1=convention-only Level#a2=convention-only Hooked#on_save=single-caller
